{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P5QuxpR2kkMsYhyGuNFEBQ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel02.1-uc001-tee\n     2→title: \"Copy stdin to stdout and files via tee\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator pipes data through the Go tee binary to capture a copy in one or more\n     6→  files while passing the stream through to stdout. The differential testing harness\n     7→  runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gtee from coreutils) with\n     8→  the same arguments, stdin, and environment, then compares stdout and output file\n     9→  contents byte-for-byte.\n    10→\n    11→actor: Human Operator\n    12→\n    13→trigger: |\n    14→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd017-tee.yaml) and invokes do-work to\n    15→  produce a passing differential test for cmd/tee.\n    16→\n    17→flow:\n    18→  - id: F1\n    19→    step: |\n    20→      The operator runs \"printf 'hello\\nworld\\n' | ./bin/tee /tmp/out.txt\". tee writes\n    21→      the data to stdout and to /tmp/out.txt simultaneously.\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      The operator runs \"printf 'line1\\n' | ./bin/tee /tmp/a.txt /tmp/b.txt\" to verify\n    25→      multi-file output. tee writes identical content to both files and stdout.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      The operator runs \"printf 'new\\n' | ./bin/tee -a /tmp/existing.txt\" to verify\n    29→      append mode. tee appends to the file without truncating existing content.\n    30→  - id: F4\n    31→    step: |\n    32→      The operator runs \"printf 'passthrough\\n' | ./bin/tee\" with no file arguments.\n    33→      tee copies stdin to stdout only (passthrough mode).\n    34→  - id: F5\n    35→    step: |\n    36→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/tee and gtee\n    37→      with the same arguments, stdin, and environment.\n    38→  - id: F6\n    39→    step: |\n    40→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte, output file contents byte-for-byte,\n    41→      and exit codes. Both binaries must produce identical results.\n    42→\n    43→touchpoints:\n    44→  - T1: \"cmd/tee — stdin copy, file output, append mode, SIGINT suppression (prd017-tee R1, R2, R3)\"\n    45→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, stdout and file comparison\"\n    46→\n    47→success_criteria:\n    48→  - id: S1\n    49→    criterion: cmd/tee compiles and ./bin/tee exists after mage build.\n    50→  - id: S2\n    51→    criterion: |\n    52→      \"printf 'hello\\nworld\\n' | ./bin/tee /tmp/out.txt\" produces \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n    53→      on stdout and identical content in /tmp/out.txt, matching gtee.\n    54→  - id: S3\n    55→    criterion: |\n    56→      Multi-file mode works: both output files contain identical content to stdout.\n    57→  - id: S4\n    58→    criterion: |\n    59→      Append mode works: \"tee -a\" appends to existing files without truncating.\n    60→  - id: S5\n    61→    criterion: |\n    62→      Passthrough mode works: tee with no file arguments copies stdin to stdout.\n    63→  - id: S6\n    64→    criterion: |\n    65→      Write-error handling works: tee exits 1 when an output file cannot be opened,\n    66→      prints a diagnostic to stderr, and continues writing to other destinations.\n    67→  - id: S7\n    68→    criterion: |\n    69→      The differential test passes for single file, multiple files, append mode,\n    70→      passthrough, and write-error cases.\n    71→\n    72→out_of_scope:\n    73→  - SIGINT suppression (-i) is tested for compilation but interactive signal delivery\n    74→    is not automated in the differential harness.\n    75→  - Output-error modes (--output-error) and -p flag are excluded per the PRD.\n    76→\n    77→test_suite: test-rel02.1\n    78→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a9684d5-9b1c-4463-9a15-9766df9bd4ee","uuid":"5a46aff7-9b12-4378-ad06-ff728c37b65c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/340/docs/specs/use-cases/rel02.1-uc001-tee.yaml","content":"id: rel02.1-uc001-tee\ntitle: \"Copy stdin to stdout and files via tee\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator pipes data through the Go tee binary to capture a copy in one or more\n  files while passing the stream through to stdout. The differential testing harness\n  runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gtee from coreutils) with\n  the same arguments, stdin, and environment, then compares stdout and output file\n  contents byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd017-tee.yaml) and invokes do-work to\n  produce a passing differential test for cmd/tee.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"printf 'hello\\nworld\\n' | ./bin/tee /tmp/out.txt\". tee writes\n      the data to stdout and to /tmp/out.txt simultaneously.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"printf 'line1\\n' | ./bin/tee /tmp/a.txt /tmp/b.txt\" to verify\n      multi-file output. tee writes identical content to both files and stdout.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"printf 'new\\n' | ./bin/tee -a /tmp/existing.txt\" to verify\n      append mode. tee appends to the file without truncating existing content.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"printf 'passthrough\\n' | ./bin/tee\" with no file arguments.\n      tee copies stdin to stdout only (passthrough mode).\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/tee and gtee\n      with the same arguments, stdin, and environment.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte, output file contents byte-for-byte,\n      and exit codes. Both binaries must produce identical results.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/tee — stdin copy, file output, append mode, SIGINT suppression (prd017-tee R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, stdout and file comparison\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/tee compiles and ./bin/tee exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: |\n      \"printf 'hello\\nworld\\n' | ./bin/tee /tmp/out.txt\" produces \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n      on stdout and identical content in /tmp/out.txt, matching gtee.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: |\n      Multi-file mode works: both output files contain identical content to stdout.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: |\n      Append mode works: \"tee -a\" appends to existing files without truncating.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: |\n      Passthrough mode works: tee with no file arguments copies stdin to stdout.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: |\n      Write-error handling works: tee exits 1 when an output file cannot be opened,\n      prints a diagnostic to stderr, and continues writing to other destinations.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test passes for single file, multiple files, append mode,\n      passthrough, and write-error cases.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - SIGINT suppression (-i) is tested for compilation but interactive signal delivery\n    is not automated in the differential harness.\n  - Output-error modes (--output-error) and -p flag are excluded per the PRD.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel02.1\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
