{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HAU7VvhewErdTpD5VPQH7r","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel02.1\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel02.1 — tee\"\n     3→release: rel02.1\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel02.1-uc001-tee\n     7→  - prd017-tee R1\n     8→  - prd017-tee R2\n     9→  - prd017-tee R3\n    10→  - prd017-tee R4\n    11→\n    12→preconditions:\n    13→  - ./bin/tee exists (built via mage build).\n    14→  - Reference binary gtee is installed via Homebrew (coreutils) and on PATH.\n    15→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/tee/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    16→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    17→  - \"tee tests create temporary files in a test-owned directory for output verification.\"\n    18→  - \"tee tests compare both stdout and output file contents between the Go and reference binaries.\"\n    19→\n    20→test_cases:\n    21→  # --- passthrough (no files) ---\n    22→  - name: tee_passthrough\n    23→    description: \"tee with no file arguments copies stdin to stdout only.\"\n    24→    inputs:\n    25→      args: []\n    26→      stdin: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n    27→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    28→    normalization: none\n    29→    expected:\n    30→      exit_code: 0\n    31→      stdout: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n    32→      stderr: \"\"\n    33→    traces:\n    34→      - prd017-tee R1.2\n    35→\n    36→  # --- single file ---\n    37→  - name: tee_single_file\n    38→    description: \"tee writes stdin to stdout and to one output file.\"\n    39→    inputs:\n    40→      args: [\"$TMPDIR/out.txt\"]\n    41→      stdin: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n    42→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    43→    normalization: none\n    44→    expected:\n    45→      exit_code: 0\n    46→      stdout: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n    47→      file_contents:\n    48→        \"$TMPDIR/out.txt\": \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n    49→      stderr: \"\"\n    50→    traces:\n    51→      - prd017-tee R1.1\n    52→      - prd017-tee R1.3\n    53→\n    54→  # --- multiple files ---\n    55→  - name: tee_multiple_files\n    56→    description: \"tee writes identical content to two output files and stdout.\"\n    57→    inputs:\n    58→      args: [\"$TMPDIR/a.txt\", \"$TMPDIR/b.txt\"]\n    59→      stdin: \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n    60→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    61→    normalization: none\n    62→    expected:\n    63→      exit_code: 0\n    64→      stdout: \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n    65→      file_contents:\n    66→        \"$TMPDIR/a.txt\": \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n    67→        \"$TMPDIR/b.txt\": \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n    68→      stderr: \"\"\n    69→    traces:\n    70→      - prd017-tee R1.1\n    71→      - prd017-tee R1.5\n    72→\n    73→  # --- append mode ---\n    74→  - name: tee_append_mode\n    75→    description: \"tee -a appends to existing file instead of truncating.\"\n    76→    inputs:\n    77→      args: [\"-a\", \"$TMPDIR/existing.txt\"]\n    78→      stdin: \"new\\n\"\n    79→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    80→      setup: \"printf 'old\\\\n' > $TMPDIR/existing.txt\"\n    81→    normalization: none\n    82→    expected:\n    83→      exit_code: 0\n    84→      stdout: \"new\\n\"\n    85→      file_contents:\n    86→        \"$TMPDIR/existing.txt\": \"old\\nnew\\n\"\n    87→      stderr: \"\"\n    88→    traces:\n    89→      - prd017-tee R2.1\n    90→\n    91→  # --- truncate by default ---\n    92→  - name: tee_truncate_default\n    93→    description: \"tee without -a truncates existing file before writing.\"\n    94→    inputs:\n    95→      args: [\"$TMPDIR/existing.txt\"]\n    96→      stdin: \"replacement\\n\"\n    97→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    98→      setup: \"printf 'original content\\\\n' > $TMPDIR/existing.txt\"\n    99→    normalization: none\n   100→    expected:\n   101→      exit_code: 0\n   102→      stdout: \"replacement\\n\"\n   103→      file_contents:\n   104→        \"$TMPDIR/existing.txt\"