UL bytes, high bytes) in both stdout and output file.\"\n   162→    inputs:\n   163→      args: [\"$TMPDIR/binary.out\"]\n   164→      stdin: \"\\\\x00\\\\x01\\\\xff\\\\n\"\n   165→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   166→    normalization: none\n   167→    expected:\n   168→      exit_code: 0\n   169→      stdout: \"\\\\x00\\\\x01\\\\xff\\\\n\"\n   170→      file_contents:\n   171→        \"$TMPDIR/binary.out\": \"\\\\x00\\\\x01\\\\xff\\\\n\"\n   172→      stderr: \"\"\n   173→    traces:\n   174→      - prd017-tee R1.5\n   175→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a9684d5-9b1c-4463-9a15-9766df9bd4ee","uuid":"ef037db9-f84c-4b94-ad99-61311ab5b8e8","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/340/docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel02.1.yaml","content":"id: test-rel02.1\ntitle: \"Test Suite: rel02.1 — tee\"\nrelease: rel02.1\n\ntraces:\n  - rel02.1-uc001-tee\n  - prd017-tee R1\n  - prd017-tee R2\n  - prd017-tee R3\n  - prd017-tee R4\n\npreconditions:\n  - ./bin/tee exists (built via mage build).\n  - Reference binary gtee is installed via Homebrew (coreutils) and on PATH.\n  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/tee/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n  - \"tee tests create temporary files in a test-owned directory for output verification.\"\n  - \"tee tests compare both stdout and output file contents between the Go and reference binaries.\"\n\ntest_cases:\n  # --- passthrough (no files) ---\n  - name: tee_passthrough\n    description: \"tee with no file arguments copies stdin to stdout only.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: []\n      stdin: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd017-tee R1.2\n\n  # --- single file ---\n  - name: tee_single_file\n    description: \"tee writes stdin to stdout and to one output file.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"$TMPDIR/out.txt\"]\n      stdin: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n      file_contents:\n        \"$TMPDIR/out.txt\": \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd017-tee R1.1\n      - prd017-tee R1.3\n\n  # --- multiple files ---\n  - name: tee_multiple_files\n    description: \"tee writes identical content to two output files and stdout.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"$TMPDIR/a.txt\", \"$TMPDIR/b.txt\"]\n      stdin: \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n      file_contents:\n        \"$TMPDIR/a.txt\": \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n        \"$TMPDIR/b.txt\": \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd017-tee R1.1\n      - prd017-tee R1.5\n\n  # --- append mode ---\n  - name: tee_append_mode\n    description: \"tee -a appends to existing file instead of truncating.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-a\", \"$TMPDIR/existing.txt\"]\n      stdin: \"new\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n      setup: \"printf 'old\\\\n' > $TMPDIR/existing.txt\"\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"new\\n\"\n      file_contents:\n        \"$TMPDIR/existing.txt\": \"old\\nnew\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd017-tee R2.1\n\n  # --- truncate by default ---\n  - name: tee_truncate_default\n    description: \"tee without -a truncates existing file before writing.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"$TMPDIR/existing.txt\"]\n      stdin: \"replacement\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n      setup: \"printf 'original content\\\\n' > $TMPDIR/existing.txt\"\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"replacement\\n\"\n      file_contents:\n        \"$TMPDIR/existing.txt\": \"replacement\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd017-tee R1.3\n\n  # --- dash as stdout ---\n  - name: tee_dash_stdout\n    description: \"tee with '-' as a file argument treats it as stdout reference; output is not duplicated.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-\"]\n      stdin: \"data\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"data\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd017-tee R1.4\n\n  # --- write error ---\n  - name: tee_write_error\n    description: \"tee exits 1 when an output file cannot be opened; continues writing to other destinations.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"/nonexistent-dir/file.txt\", \"$TMPDIR/good.txt\"]\n      stdin: \"data\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 1\n      stdout: \"data\\n\"\n      file_contents:\n        \"$TMPDIR/good.txt\": \"data\\n\"\n      stderr: \"non-empty error message\"\n    traces:\n      - prd017-tee R3.2\n      - prd017-tee R3.3\n\n  # --- empty stdin ---\n  - name: tee_empty_stdin\n    description: \"tee with empty stdin creates an empty output file and produces no stdout.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"$TMPDIR/empty.txt\"]\n      stdin: \"\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"\"\n      file_contents:\n        \"$TMPDIR/empty.txt\": \"\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd017-tee R1.1\n\n  # --- binary data passthrough ---\n  - name: tee_binary_passthrough\n    description: \"tee preserves binary data (NUL bytes, high bytes) in both stdout and output file.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"$TMPDIR/binary.out\"]\n      stdin: \"\\\\x00\\\\x01\\\\xff\\\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"\\\\x00\\\\x01\\\\xff\\\\n\"\n      file_contents:\n        \"$TMPDIR/binary.out\": \"\\\\x00\\\\x01\\\\xff\\\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n     